Data Storage and Processing Specification
Version: 2026-05-21
Project: CogniPlatforms / Cognicode website + secure portal prototype

1) Purpose
This document explains where data is currently stored, how it is processed, and the target regional data model for compliance discussions (Mainland China / Hong Kong / Europe / North America).

2) Current Implementation (Prototype)
2.1 Frontend storage (browser localStorage/sessionStorage)
- Main file: secure-portal/app.js
- Current user/business data is stored in browser localStorage (prototype behavior)
- Session state is stored in sessionStorage

2.2 localStorage keys (implemented)
- portal_pending_verify_users_v2
- portal_pending_review_users_v2
- portal_approved_users_v2
- portal_m_pending_verify_users_v1
- portal_m_pending_review_users_v1
- portal_m_approved_users_v1
- portal_rewards_wallet_v1
- portal_referral_leads_v1
- portal_service_orders_v1
- portal_service_catalog_v1

2.3 sessionStorage keys (implemented)
- portal_session_user_v1
- portal_m_session_user_v1

2.4 Server-side email processing (Cloudflare Pages Functions)
Location: secure-portal/functions/api/
- send-registration-notice.js
- send-access-link.js
- send-inquiry.js
- send-points-action.js
- send-verification-code.js (added)

Email provider:
- Resend API (via env.RESEND_API_KEY)
- Sender from env.FROM_EMAIL

3) Registration / Verification / Review Flow (Current)
3.1 Enterprise user
- Submit registration form
- System generates verification code
- Verification code is emailed to registrant (send-verification-code)
- After email verification, record moves to pending review
- Admin approval moves user to approved list
- Approved user receives access link email (send-access-link)

3.2 Manufacturer user
- Same sequence as enterprise registration with manufacturer data fields

4) Points Logic (Current)
4.1 Registration reward
- On enterprise approval: +500 points to newly approved user

4.2 Referral reward
- Referrer submits CIO referral lead
- Referral does NOT grant immediate points
- When referred email account is approved, referrer gets +200 points

4.3 Service order / redemption
- Order confirmation consumes points
- Redemption consumes points according to configured catalog

5) Data Fields Involved (PII)
Common PII fields currently collected:
- fullName
- company
- jobTitle
- officePhone
- mobilePhone
- email
- region
- optional notes and inquiry details

6) Current Storage Location Summary
- User master data: browser localStorage (user device only; not centralized)
- Session data: browser sessionStorage
- Notification/verification/access emails: processed server-side by Cloudflare Functions + Resend
- No centralized production database yet in current prototype

7) Compliance Gap (Prototype vs Production)
Current prototype is not yet sufficient for formal compliance operations because:
- Data is local to browser/device (not centrally governed)
- No centralized retention/deletion workflow
- No formal audit trail for admin operations
- No region-based storage isolation implemented yet

8) Recommended Target Regional Model
8.1 Mainland China users
- Store registration and PII in China mainland infrastructure (e.g., Tencent Cloud / CloudBase CN region)

8.2 Hong Kong users
- Store in Hong Kong or international region (separate from Mainland CN data pool)

8.3 Europe users
- Prefer EU region storage/processing and GDPR-aligned controls

8.4 North America users
- Store in NA region with equivalent privacy controls and contract governance

9) Minimum Production Controls Required
- Region-based routing at registration entry
- Centralized database (no browser-only persistence)
- RBAC for admin/superuser roles
- Audit logs for approvals/exports/role changes
- Data retention policy + deletion workflow
- Subject access/export/deletion request process
- Cross-border transfer records and legal basis documentation

10) Current Contacts for Enterprise Service
- ITsupport@cogniplatforms.com

11) Notes
- This document reflects implemented behavior as of 2026-05-21.
- If architecture is migrated to CloudBase/Tencent CN + global stack, update this spec and version number.
